            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Doug Matthews"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have also been tweaking this recipe some by adding an extra quarter cup of cornmeal and substituting buttermilk for regular milk - it gives it a cakier appearance and moistens it a little. I can't leave well enough alone. Thanks."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RedYak3867"
            },
            "reviewBody": "You can't go wrong with this basic recipe. However, I substitute the milk with organic coconut milk, the canola with grassfed butter, and the sugar with Monk fruit sugar alternative. I also make sure to use Organic Unbleached Flour, Organic Cornmeal, and Organic Pasture Raised eggs. In addition, I double the recipe in order to fill a stainless steel muffin pan with 6 large receptacles... Oh, and I had to add extra time. It took these large muffins a total of 30 minutes to bake with me checking every 5 mins of the extra time by inserting a butter knife. Enjoy!",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-27T15:24:10.274Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the recipe as given with only one exception; I used coconut oil. I love these. There was only enough batter to make 9 muffins in a standard muffin pan. (Each cup filled half way) I don't find them to be bland as some have said, but rather tasty in a simplistic way. I baked for 15 minutes at 200°C and they are perfectly moist. Don't over bake. Serve with butter. It is, as some have said, a great recipe to start with if you want to get creative.",
            "datePublished": "2024-09-09T14:20:13.047Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RWC4520"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were delicious! I like the equal proportions of flour and corn meal. I made 1.5 recipes, and it made 14 large muffins. I soured the milk with white vinegar to give them more lift. I scooped the batter into silicone baking cups (one of the best inventions ever!) and let the batter rest for 15 minutes before putting them in the oven.",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-31T22:24:30.545Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "UpbeatEel6559"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I prefer to use 1/4 c sugar, less sweet, like cornbread. Using a metal muffin tin in an electric oven, cooking time was shorter; 12-15 min. I make it with almond milk and organic ingredients.",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-18T18:26:49.800Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ellen D"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like this basic recipe very much. I use 1/4 melted butter instead of oil for a richer taste, 1/2 cup applesauce instead of egg since I don't eat eggs, and I add 1/2 cup of corn for texture. Occasionally, I've also added 2 tbl of jalapeños for a bit of spice!",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-27T15:42:37.048Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I put in a can of creamed corn in the mix!!! Also used self rising white corn meal!!! Yummy!!!",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-09T10:37:03.872Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
